      "command": "npm run check:runtime-asset-store-local",
      "requiredWorkflows": [
        ".github/workflows/runtime-native.yml"
      ],
      "notes": "Pins the private principal-bound local Asset store, its exact SQLite schema/configuration/source/dependency inventory, transactional write and bounded-read evidence, Rust 1.89 metadata, and native-only isolation from WASM, C ABI, W7a, Electron IPC, activation, and capability advertisement. The sibling workflow runs its tests and Clippy from an isolated clean target on Windows, macOS, and Linux.",
      "intentionallySplit": true,
      "escalatable": true
    },
    {
      "npmScript": "check:runtime-asset-host-local",
      "command": "npm run check:runtime-asset-host-local",
      "requiredWorkflows": [
        ".github/workflows/runtime-native.yml"
      ],
      "notes": "Pins the private native-only local Asset host, its exact source and dependency closure, its byte-identical approved texture-plan schema copy, the exact reviewed resolver/store consumer edges, Rust 1.89 metadata, bounded in-process materialization/resolution, exact normalized manifest-closure ingestion with at most nine supplied objects and a descriptor-last logical commit, activation-plan preflight, and continued isolation from language bridges, C ABI, WASM, W7a/Electron wiring, GPU/runtime activation, and capability advertisement. Expected-reference kind/size/media preflight precedes closure inspection. Validation and caller-derived Asset failures occur before writes; chunk or manifest write failures never attempt the descriptor; a Store error after descriptor insertion is attempted is outcome-ambiguous and the immutable operation is retryable. An impossible durable-parser divergence during publication is redacted to Store without a stable Asset code. These are per-call validation bounds, not a caller quota, rate limit, concurrency policy, or exact total peak-memory guarantee. Raw-JSON parsing, duplicate-key rejection, and Stage 1 schema validation for typed texture plans remain bridge-owned; manifest ingestion reuses the resolver's approved bounded duplicate-aware Stage 1/Stage 2 parser. The sibling workflow runs its focused tests and Clippy from an isolated clean target on Windows, macOS, and Linux.",
      "intentionallySplit": true,
      "escalatable": true
    },
    {
      "npmScript": "check:runtime-native-evaluation",
      "command": "npm run check:runtime-native-evaluation",
      "requiredWorkflows": [
        ".github/workflows/runtime-native.yml"
      ],
      "notes": "Pins the private consumer-zero Evaluation Payload v1 validation foundation, its byte-identical approved model schema copy, and approved-schema reachable accepted-set parity through one shared AJV/Rust corpus without claiming generic JSON Schema branch coverage beyond that artifact. It pins duplicate-aware transport ceilings of 67,108,864 raw bytes, depth 64, 8,000,000 JSON tokens, and 67,108,864 UTF-8 bytes per decoded string. Stage 1 rejects unknown structural fields before Stage 2 semantics; producer-side forbidden scanning is outside this crate, while opaque skins, bindPoseInverse, and expression-values keys remain data. It pins finite, binary64-normalized numeric values without source-number-lexeme or negative-zero preservation and without f32 storage or casts, the full opaque u64 request-generation range, stable texture-binding inventory using atlas:<sourceAtlasId> in UTF-8 byte order, and the Runtime Spec v1.0 loader-preflight policy that rejects nonempty clips or stateMachines as unsupported after both validation stages. Success is only a validated, inventory-bearing loader-preflight candidate, not a generic schema-valid payload parser; it is eligible for future lowering or activation only after A-09 is resolved. Explicit fallible reservations and ceilings do not promise recoverable handling for every hidden serde_json::Map or serializer allocation failure. It also pins dependency license/checksum closure, Rust 1.89 metadata, native tests and Clippy, rustdoc with warnings denied, and wasm32 compile and Clippy evidence. It remains disconnected from runtime-native core, C ABI/editor symbols and headers, WASM exports, language or IPC bridges, filesystem and network I/O, unsafe code, f32 lowering or evaluation, Asset activation, GPU upload, and capability advertisement; A-09 and EDH-01 remain open.",
      "intentionallySplit": true,
      "escalatable": true
